UPDATE firms SET about = 'Blottman Legal Services is an Ontario firm focused on traffic and driving-related charges, including driving under suspension, careless driving, and other Highway Traffic Act matters. The firm offers 24/7 intake for new traffic charges and represents clients across Ontario courts. Leslie Rivas, a licensed paralegal with the firm, has represented clients on Highway Traffic Act matters including hand-held communication device charges.' WHERE slug = 'blottman-legal-services' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Barbarian Law is an Aurora-based firm handling residential and commercial real estate closings, along with corporate, commercial, wills and estates, and fractional general counsel work. The firm has closed over 1,000 client transactions and quotes fees up front before a purchase, sale, or refinance closes.' WHERE slug = 'barbarian-law' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Hoare Claxton Criminal Defence is a Calgary firm that focuses on criminal charges. Clients may also know it by its earlier name, Ouellette Hoare Claxton, under which it announced its Calgary criminal defence services in March 2022. The office is at 600 6th Avenue SW, Suite 210.The firm says it represents people charged under the Criminal Code of Canada or provincial statutes. Its published descriptions mention assault, theft, drug, weapons and impaired driving offences, as well as domestic violence, sexual offences and serious charges. It offers personalized advice and describes an approach built on protecting clients’ rights at every stage of a case. Call the office to ask whether it can take your matter.' WHERE slug = 'hoare-claxton-criminal-defence' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Cuming & Gillespie is a Calgary boutique that acts exclusively for plaintiffs with serious injury claims, including motor vehicle collisions, slip-and-fall injuries, securities litigation and medical negligence. It also acts in class actions.In a 2019 Canadian Lawyer feature, partner James Cuming said the firm takes on more serious injuries and fewer clients, and focuses on recovery, such as arranging occupational therapy and the right treating specialists, rather than only maximizing a claim. The firm has said it acted as counsel in Alberta’s first certified class action and that it is counsel for the Province of Alberta in the health-cost recovery claims against tobacco manufacturers. Best suited to people with serious or catastrophic injuries.' WHERE slug = 'cuming-gillespie-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Parlee McLaws traces its history to the 1880s, when Sir James Lougheed opened a Calgary office, followed by an Edmonton office; the two practices merged in 1986 to form Parlee McLaws. Its alumni include Prime Minister R.B. Bennett and Senator James Lougheed. The firm has offices at Enbridge Centre in Edmonton and in the TD Canada Trust Tower in Calgary.Parlee McLaws lists a broad range of practice areas, including corporate and commercial law, securities, litigation, real estate, labour and employment, intellectual property, energy, insolvency, administrative law and online brand protection, with patent and trademark agents on the team. It joined the USLAW network as Alberta’s member firm in 2025 and became a collaborating firm of Andersen Global in February 2026. Typically suits businesses and individuals across Alberta.' WHERE slug = 'parlee-mclaws-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'McCarthy Tétrault’s Calgary office is where much of the firm’s national oil and gas practice is run, according to Chambers. It works from the TD Canada Trust Tower on 7th Avenue SW as part of the firm’s national Business Law Group.Lawyers there focus on oil and gas, power, renewables and energy-transition work, together with infrastructure, regulatory, environmental and Indigenous law, and the office has its own litigation group, whose practice lead concentrates on corporate-commercial disputes in the energy industry. In June 2026 the firm added a regulatory partner in Calgary and described continued investment in the Calgary market. Typically suits energy and infrastructure companies.' WHERE slug = 'mccarthy-t-trault-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Norton Rose Fulbright’s Calgary office grew out of Macleod Dixon, a Calgary firm with close to a century of roots that combined with Norton Rose Canada on January 1, 2012. The wider firm is a global practice with offices in more than 50 cities; in Canada it also has offices in Montréal, Ottawa, Québec City, Toronto and Vancouver.Macleod Dixon was regarded as a specialist in energy and mining work, and it brought offices in Latin America and Central Asia into the merged firm. Energy and infrastructure, and mining and commodities, remain central to the Canadian practice. The Calgary office is on 3rd Avenue SW. Typically suits energy and resource companies with cross-border operations.' WHERE slug = 'norton-rose-fulbright-canada-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Osler is a national business law firm with offices in Toronto, Montréal, Calgary, Vancouver, Ottawa and New York. Its Calgary office is in Brookfield Place on 6th Avenue SW, and in a 2021 interview the office’s managing partner said most of its lawyers are from Western Canada.Energy anchors the Calgary practice: Osler’s national Energy Group is ranked Band 1 in Chambers Canada, and the office acts on oil and gas, LNG, power and renewable projects. The same office points to depth in technology, emerging and high-growth companies, and agribusiness. In 2025 the firm added two energy M&A partners in Calgary. Typically suits companies, investors and institutions with complex transactions.' WHERE slug = 'osler-hoskin-harcourt-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Torys opened its Calgary office in March 2011 with seven partners, mainly to serve clients in the energy sector. The office is on the 46th floor of Eighth Avenue Place East. Torys was founded in Toronto in 1941 and also has offices in New York, Montréal and Halifax.The firm says Calgary clients include major corporations as well as entrepreneurs, cannabis growers, oil and gas and power companies, pension and investment funds, renewable energy generators, technology companies and government. Legal 500 notes Calgary-based strength in energy-related debt finance and in securities compliance and corporate finance. Typically suits companies and investors with cross-border or capital-markets work.' WHERE slug = 'torys-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Stikeman Elliott’s Calgary office is in Bankers Hall West and is home to the firm’s Oil & Gas Group, which combines Calgary-based expertise with the firm’s international relationships. Stikeman also has offices in Montréal, Toronto, Ottawa, Vancouver, New York and London.Calgary lawyers work in commercial energy, corporate and M&A, and projects and infrastructure, across upstream, midstream, downstream and power, with newer work in renewable natural gas, hydrogen and carbon capture. Legal 500 describes the oil and gas practice’s transactional offering as spanning M&A, finance and project development. The office also has a regulatory group. Typically suits energy companies and their investors.' WHERE slug = 'stikeman-elliott-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Walsh LLP was established in Calgary in 1959 by Thomas Walsh, who went on to serve as a bencher of the Law Society of Alberta and as president of the Canadian Bar Association. The firm has offices in Calgary, Canmore, Claresholm, Okotoks and Stand Off, and says it has worked with almost every Alberta industry for over 60 years.Walsh describes a people-first approach that runs from farm and family law to corporate and commercial work and civil litigation, and its services also include wills and estates, real estate, municipal, regulatory and public law, and First Nations law. It calls itself a mid-sized firm, and it has the largest Google review count of the Alberta firms listed here. Typically suits families, farms and small and mid-sized businesses.' WHERE slug = 'walsh-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Burnet, Duckworth & Palmer, or BD&P, was founded in 1905 and is headquartered in Calgary. It describes itself as a full-service boutique of about 120 lawyers who work on corporate and litigation matters opposite national and international firms.Clients come from energy, renewables, agribusiness, technology and life sciences. Practice areas the firm lists include corporate and commercial law, energy, mergers and acquisitions, securities, tax, litigation, employment, real estate, aviation, technology and Indigenous law. In August 2026 BD&P was named Alberta’s representative in the Alliott Global Alliance. Typically suits Alberta-based businesses that want an independent Calgary firm.' WHERE slug = 'burnet-duckworth-palmer-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Bennett Jones was founded in Calgary in 1922 and says it has been part of the city’s business life for more than a century. Its early history is tied to R.B. Bennett, who went on to become Canada’s 11th prime minister, and the firm remains the principal legal advisor to the Calgary Stampede.The Calgary office, in Bankers Hall East, offers corporate, litigation, regulatory and environmental, and tax services. The firm says its lawyers drafted some of the first oil field contracts after the 1947 Leduc discovery, and energy, mining, funds and finance, and capital projects are among its major practice areas. It also has offices elsewhere in Canada and in New York. Its work is aimed at companies, investors and institutions rather than individual consumer matters.' WHERE slug = 'bennett-jones-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Bryan & Company has practised in Edmonton since 1928 and says it now has more than 40 lawyers in the provincial capital. It describes itself as grounded in Alberta roots but serving clients globally, and its lawyers are members of the International Alliance of Law Firms.The firm offers what it calls the full breadth of services regardless of industry, and its published profile highlights corporate law, commercial litigation and real estate. It works from Manulife Place on 101 Street NW. Typically suits Alberta businesses and property clients that want a mid-size Edmonton firm.' WHERE slug = 'bryan-and-company-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Borden Ladner Gervais, or BLG, has five offices: Vancouver, Calgary, Toronto, Ottawa and Montréal. The firm says its roots go back to 1823 and that it is fully bilingual in English and French across practice areas. The Calgary practice traces its own history to Howard Mackie, founded in 1888.From the East Tower of Centennial Place on 3rd Avenue SW, BLG’s Calgary lawyers list commercial litigation, securities, construction, commercial real estate, financial services, employment and energy law among their strengths. Lexpert also lists the Calgary office as repeatedly recommended in asset and equipment finance. Typically suits businesses that want national coverage with a Calgary team.' WHERE slug = 'borden-ladner-gervais-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'MLT Aikins traces its history to 1879 and Sir James Aikins, and is the product of a merger between MacPherson Leslie & Tyerman and Aikins, MacAulay & Thorvaldson. It has more than 300 lawyers and offices across the four western provinces, including Vancouver, Edmonton, Calgary, Saskatoon, Regina and Winnipeg.The Calgary office opened in 2002 and now has more than 60 lawyers, working in energy and environmental law, intellectual property, commercial litigation, agribusiness, corporate finance and commercial real estate. Lexpert lists the office as most frequently recommended in Aboriginal law and repeatedly recommended in insolvency and restructuring and technology transactions. Typically suits western Canadian businesses that want a single firm across provinces.' WHERE slug = 'mlt-aikins-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Dentons Canada has offices in Vancouver, Edmonton, Calgary, Toronto, Ottawa and Montréal, and traces its Canadian roots to 1839 in Toronto and 1888 in Edmonton. The Calgary office is on the 15th floor of Bankers Court on 2nd Street SW, and the firm is part of Dentons, which describes itself as the world’s largest law firm.Dentons’ national Energy group has been adding to its Calgary bench, including a senior energy partner who joined in February 2026. The firm lists more than 40 practice areas and highlights energy, mining, financial services, infrastructure, technology and real estate. Thomson Reuters Market Insights has recognized it in Canada for cross-border deals and cross-border litigation. Typically suits companies and institutions.' WHERE slug = 'dentons-canada-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Blake, Cassels & Graydon, known as Blakes, has served Alberta’s business community from Calgary for more than four decades. The firm says the office acts on some of Canada’s largest and most complex transactions, major cross-border deals and “bet-the-company” disputes.Calgary lawyers cover corporate and commercial, securities, oil and gas, electricity, tax, banking and finance, real estate, litigation, restructuring, employment, environmental and regulatory work. The firm’s Oil & Gas group is headquartered in the Calgary office, and Legal 500 has described Blakes as a first port of call for many oil and gas transactions. Chambers also recognizes the Calgary group for energy-industry disputes and securities litigation. Typically suits companies and institutions.' WHERE slug = 'blake-cassels-graydon-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Witten LLP describes itself as an Edmonton-based full-service firm with a legacy of nearly a century, with just over 50 lawyers and articling students combined and about 100 staff. Its office is in Canadian Western Bank Place on Jasper Avenue.The firm lists business law, litigation, real estate, Indigenous law and employment law among its practice areas, and it has a Condominium Management Group that advises condominium corporations, directors, property managers and owners. Best Lawyers recognizes its lawyers in areas including public procurement, Indigenous law, corporate, real estate, commercial litigation and trusts and estates. Typically suits homeowners, condominium boards, businesses and public bodies.' WHERE slug = 'witten-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Field Law is a western and northern regional business law firm with offices in Edmonton, Calgary and Yellowknife. Its Edmonton office traces its roots to 1915 and a firm called Woods, Sherry, Collison & Field, and its Calgary office to 1921. In 2015 it expanded into Northern Canada and says it became the largest law firm serving the Northwest Territories.More than 120 lawyers work across corporate and commercial matters, litigation, labour and employment, insurance, intellectual property, energy, occupational health and safety, privacy, professional regulatory issues and medical malpractice issues. For individuals the firm also provides estate planning and real estate transactions. Its Edmonton office is on 101 Street NW. Typically suits organizations and businesses, with services for individuals as well.' WHERE slug = 'field-law' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Duncan Craig traces its origins to 1894 with founding partners William Short, later Edmonton’s first mayor, and Charles Cross, who became Alberta’s first Attorney General. Its head office is on Jasper Avenue in downtown Edmonton, it has a second office in Drayton Valley, and it says it has about 45 lawyers.Practice areas include estate, family, personal injury, real estate, employment, business, commercial litigation, banking, insolvency, insurance, intellectual property, construction, agribusiness, surface rights and Indigenous law. The firm was ranked among the top 10 law firms in Alberta in Canadian Lawyer’s Top Western Law Firms 2025–26 and says it was named nationally Tier 1 in trusts and estates in the 2025 Best Law Firms Canada rankings. Typically suits individuals, families and businesses across Alberta.' WHERE slug = 'duncan-craig-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'McLennan Ross was founded in Edmonton in 1903 and opened a Yellowknife office in 1999, building what it describes as the largest labour and employment practice in the Northwest Territories. It has more than 100 lawyers in Edmonton, Calgary and Yellowknife.Its Edmonton office is in its own building on Stony Plain Road NW, west of the downtown core. Areas the firm lists include employment and labour, municipal and governmental services, energy, construction, education and health, plus tax, privacy, professional liability, workplace investigations and wealth advisory work. Chambers Canada has recognized it for general business law in Northern Canada and the Arctic. Typically suits employers, public bodies and businesses.' WHERE slug = 'mclennan-ross-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Brownlee LLP is a mid-sized regional firm with offices in Edmonton and Calgary, serving clients across Alberta and in Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut. It names civil litigation, municipal and administrative law, and corporate-commercial law as its core strengths, and its Edmonton office is in Commerce Place on 102 Street NW.The firm’s job postings describe a significant volume of business and real estate development work for public sector clients such as municipalities, utility providers, school boards and post-secondary institutions, alongside private businesses. Court reports show its lawyers in matters before the Alberta Utilities Commission and the Court of Appeal of Alberta, and in construction and insurance disputes. Typically suits municipalities, public bodies and businesses.' WHERE slug = 'brownlee-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Reynolds Mirth Richards & Farmer, known as RMRF, has served clients from Edmonton since 1915. The firm says its lawyers have been appointed to the Supreme Court of Canada, the Court of Appeal of Alberta, the Court of Queen’s Bench, the Provincial Court of Alberta and the Supreme Court of the Northwest Territories. Its office is in the Stantec Tower on 103 Avenue NW.RMRF lists administrative and public law, alternative dispute resolution, construction, corporate and commercial litigation, corporate law, defamation and media law, expropriation, health care, insolvency, insurance, intellectual property, labour and employment, municipal law, real estate, and trusts and estates. It says it has worked closely with the construction industry for over 50 years. Typically suits businesses, public bodies and individuals with a dispute.' WHERE slug = 'reynolds-mirth-richards-farmer-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Miller Thomson’s Calgary office grew from two founding partners in 1987 to nearly fifty lawyers. It is on the 43rd floor of Eighth Avenue Place East, near 8th Avenue and 4th Street SW, and the firm has an Edmonton office as well. Nationally Miller Thomson has about 500 lawyers across five provinces.Services the Calgary office highlights include capital markets and securities, commercial litigation, construction litigation and corporate tax, and Lexpert lists both the Calgary and Edmonton offices as repeatedly recommended in banking and financial institutions. The firm says it combines national expertise with local knowledge of Alberta’s leading industries. Typically suits mid-sized and larger businesses.' WHERE slug = 'miller-thomson-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Gowling WLG’s Calgary office has operated locally for almost 50 years and describes itself as one of the largest groups of legal professionals in Western Canada. The firm traces its roots to 1887 and became Gowling WLG in February 2016, when Canada’s Gowlings combined with the UK’s Wragge Lawrence Graham & Co.Calgary lawyers work in energy, restructuring and insolvency, and commercial litigation, and the firm’s national Energy Group covers oil and gas, renewables, electricity and nuclear. Firm-wide the practice also spans real estate, employment, tax, technology and Indigenous law. Lexpert lists the Calgary office as repeatedly recommended in Indigenous (Aboriginal) law. The office is on 7th Avenue SW. Typically suits businesses, lenders and public bodies.' WHERE slug = 'gowling-wlg-canada-llp-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Bishop & McKenzie describes itself as a regional law firm that has operated in Alberta for more than 120 years. Its Calgary office is at 605 5th Avenue SW; the firm also has an Edmonton office on 101 Street NW.Topics the firm publishes on include litigation, mediation and arbitration, family and matrimonial law, insolvency and restructuring, tax, employment, privacy and technology. Court reports show its lawyers appearing in the Court of King’s Bench of Alberta and the Court of Appeal of Alberta on commercial, construction, real estate and condominium disputes. Typically suits businesses and individuals with a dispute or a transaction.' WHERE slug = 'bishop-mckenzie-llp' AND about IS NULL;
UPDATE firms SET about = 'Fasken’s Calgary practice, in First Canadian Centre on 7th Avenue SW, says it mirrors the Alberta market with experience in energy, oil and gas, mining, real estate, banking, finance, infrastructure, technology, Indigenous affairs and government. Firm-wide it has more than 900 lawyers in ten offices, including London and Johannesburg.Fasken also has an office in Tsuut’ina, Alberta, alongside Calgary. Chambers describes the firm’s energy and environment group as advising on energy projects, First Nations agreements, financings and carbon markets, and says Fasken has an unparalleled reputation in mining. Its services are pitched from start-ups to global corporations entering the Canadian market. Typically suits energy, mining and infrastructure companies.' WHERE slug = 'fasken-calgary' AND about IS NULL;
